# npm workspaces

This repo is an npm workspaces monorepo. Install a package in the **workspace that imports it**, never in the root `package.json` unless the exception below applies.

## Where packages go

| Package kind | Location |
| --- | --- |
| NestJS, TypeORM, `class-validator`, `class-transformer`, backend test libs | `backend/package.json` |
| Next.js, React, Tailwind, frontend test libs | `frontend/package.json` |
| Repo-wide tooling used from root scripts (e.g. Prettier) | root `package.json` `devDependencies` |
| npm `overrides` / `engines` / `workspaces` | root `package.json` only |

## Commands

From the **repository root**:

```bash
npm install <pkg> --workspace backend
npm install <pkg> --workspace frontend
npm install -D <pkg> --workspace backend
```

Do **not** run `npm install <pkg>` at the root (that writes root `dependencies`).
Do **not** add Nest or Next libraries to root `dependencies` so Docker or hoisting “finds” them.

## Root `package.json` may contain

- `workspaces`, `scripts`, `engines`
- Shared format/lint CLIs invoked from root scripts
- `overrides` for transitive security pins

If both apps need the same library, still install it in **each** workspace. Do not hoist it to the root to “share” it.
